# License scope

This repository contains separately licensed proof sources, restricted library
caches and third-party reference materials. It is not licensed as a whole under
MIT. Licenses apply only to rights that the relevant copyright holders can grant.

## Original paper proof sources

The original Lean 4 formalization code in `papers/<paper>/proof/src/`, including
its supporting proof modules, is licensed under [MIT](LICENSES/MIT.txt).
Here `<paper>` means each paper directory; the grant covers its `.lean` files
recursively, and only their original contributions. You may use, modify,
redistribute and commercially reuse that code, subject to the MIT notice
requirements. Existing third-party notices and rights remain in effect.

This source-code grant does not cover imported libraries, compiled library
caches, source articles, or other input materials. Importing Statlib does not
make Statlib part of this MIT grant. Running or distributing a proof with Statlib
still requires compliance with the applicable Statlib license; commercial use
of the original proof source does not authorize commercial use of Statlib.

## Compiled built-in library caches

The Statlib `.olean` files supplied in task `proof/cache/` directories and in
`verification/statlib-cache/` are compiled results of the built-in dependency
library. They are separate from the paper authors' input materials and from the
original paper proof sources licensed above.

These supplied caches are available only for noncommercial reproduction and
verification of the results in this repository under the
[Cache Verification License](LICENSES/CACHE-VERIFICATION.txt). This license
prohibits commercial use, extraction for reuse in other projects, and reverse
engineering to recover or reconstruct library content. Ordinary use of Lean and
the supplied verification tools to check the archived proofs is permitted.

The restriction concerns the supplied library caches, not `.olean` files that
you generate from the MIT-licensed original proof sources themselves.
It does not remove rights independently granted by an applicable upstream
license or rights that cannot lawfully be restricted.

## Upstream dependencies and library sources

Statlib remains a separately licensed upstream dependency. A copy of its
[Noncommercial Source-Available License, version 1.0](LICENSES/Statlib.txt)
is included. That upstream license permits qualifying noncommercial extensions
and requires a separate written license for commercial use; it does not turn
Statlib into MIT-licensed software. The Statlib implementation sources under
`statlib-contributions/neural-network-approximation/Statlib/` are excluded from
the paper-source MIT grant. The license applicable to the corresponding
upstream version controls; this notice does not retroactively relicense
previously released versions or replace independent upstream grants.

Lean, Mathlib and other third-party dependencies retain their respective
licenses. In particular, Mathlib is licensed under
[Apache License 2.0](https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
Any independently granted upstream rights continue to apply to upstream
material in source or compiled form; the cache restrictions do not override them.
The AxiomMath input material retains the `LICENSE.AxiomMath` notices included
in the relevant `imo-2026/problem*/input/` directories.

## Papers and other input materials

Paper PDFs, author TeX sources, figures and other input materials, including
those in `input/` and `materials/`, are excluded from the paper-source MIT grant.
Their authors, publishers and other rightsholders retain their rights under
the applicable article or material license. The papers are cited as mathematical
references and the inputs identify the statements being formalized. This
repository grants no additional permission to redistribute, sell, commercially
exploit or otherwise reuse those materials, and does not claim ownership of them.
See each paper README for its bibliographic citation.

Other repository files are not covered by the paper-source MIT grant unless
separately stated. Preserve any applicable existing notices and licenses.
